    rdfs:label "2026".
_:b0_r7b0 crm:P2_has_type <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    crm:P75i_is_possessed_by mca:sun-and-rain-works;
    a crm:E30_Right;
    rdfs:label "CC BY 4.0".
_:b0_r7b1 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Evidence archive: documentation photographs of the Ansel Adams print (August 2008)";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300404670;
    crm:P72_has_language aat:300388277;
    a crm:E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation.
_:b0_r7b2 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "record:evidence-consignment-photographs-2008";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300312355;
    a crm:E42_Identifier.
_:b0_r7b3 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Evidence status: independently checkable. Unlike the studio's correspondence and receipts, this record can be tested by any third party without access to private material. The public Sotheby's catalogue entry for sale N08533, lot 16, at https://www.sothebys.com/en/auctions/ecatalogue/2009/photographs-n08533/lot.16.html describes the print as carrying the photographer's 'Photograph by Ansel Adams for The American Trust Company' stamp, as numbered 1-SF-46, as titled, and as annotated 'Wells Fargo Bank' in ink on the reverse by the photographer; the catalogue note explains the annotation as Adams's own correction following the 1960 merger of The American Trust Company into Wells Fargo Bank. Each of those particulars is visible in the studio's 2008 verso photograph, which is published with this record, except that the negative number is legible only as far as '1-SF-' before the right edge of the frame cuts it off; the catalogue's '46' is therefore not visible and is not claimed here. A vertical crease runs through the mount to the left of the number but does not obscure it. The correspondence is therefore in four particulars - the credit stamp, the negative-number series, the inked Wells Fargo annotation over the struck-through article, and the handwritten title - and is not dependent on the studio's own account.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r7b4 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Embedded image metadata, as recorded by the camera: all eleven files carry Exif written at capture by a FUJIFILM FinePix1300, reporting the firmware string 'Digital Camera FinePix1300 Ver1.24'. Exif DateTimeOriginal values run from 2008-08-08 00:05:33 to 2008-08-08 00:10:22, a continuous session of under five minutes. The frames are numbered DSCF0012 to DSCF0017 and DSCF0020 to DSCF0024; frames 0018 and 0019 are absent from the sequence. This metadata is written by the camera at exposure and is independent of the filesystem timestamps of the storage medium, which agree with it. It remains studio-held and is not notarized: no checksums, file hashes, or custody identifiers are published at this time, and Exif fields can in principle be altered.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r7b5 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Contemporaneous conceptual intent. One frame in the sequence, exposed at 2008-08-08 00:08:46, shows the print photographed together with a copy of 'The Philosophy of Andy Warhol (From A to B and Back Again)', stood upright and facing the camera on the same ground. Sun & Rain Works reads this juxtaposition as a deliberate art-referential gesture made at the time of documentation, and as the earliest dated trace of the thinking that became The Auction as Artwork. The scope of that reading should be stated plainly: the photograph evidences that the two objects were deliberately composed in one frame in August 2008. It is not a written designation, it does not by itself establish that the auction engagement was framed as art in 2008 or 2009, and the conceptual designation remains an assertion by the artist made explicit over time.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r7b6 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Limits of the correspondence. Ansel Adams produced multiple prints from the 1952 negative, so agreement on the verso markings identifies a print of the same issue and annotation state rather than establishing a unique object beyond question; the strength of the match rests on the combination of particulars, not on any one of them. The photographs show that the print was in the room in which they were taken; the attribution of that room and camera to Sun & Rain Works rests on the studio's custody of the storage medium. The Sotheby's catalogue names no consignor, as is standard auction practice, so the identity of the consignor of record is not established here and is addressed separately in the auction-engagement evidence record.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r7b7 crm:P14_carried_out_by mca:sun-and-rain-works;
    crm:P4_has_time-span _:b0_r7b8;
    a crm:E65_Creation;
    rdfs:label "Compilation of the 2008 documentation-photograph evidence record".
_:b0_r7b8 crm:P82a_begin_of_the_begin "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>;
    crm:P82b_end_of_the_end "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>;
    a crm:E52_Time-Span;
    rdfs:label "2026".
_:b0_r8b0 crm:P2_has_type <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    crm:P75i_is_possessed_by mca:sun-and-rain-works;
    a crm:E30_Right;
    rdfs:label "CC BY 4.0".
_:b0_r8b1 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Evidence archive: Sun & Rain Works auction engagement (2009)";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300404670;
    crm:P72_has_language aat:300388277;
    a crm:E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation.
_:b0_r8b2 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "record:evidence-live-auction-2009";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300312355;
    a crm:E42_Identifier.
_:b0_r8b3 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Evidence status: mixed. Independently verifiable: (1) the public Sotheby's catalogue lot (sale N08533, lot 16) at https://www.sothebys.com/en/auctions/ecatalogue/2009/photographs-n08533/lot.16.html ; (2) a Sun and Rain Works public post carrying the 'WTF is Art' theme (X post 373257603108704256). Its date is confirmed independently by the platform's timestamp-encoded ID, which decodes to 2013-08-30T01:35:22Z — that is 2013-08-29 at 15:35 in Hawaii-Aleutian Standard Time, the studio's local time, and the post is dated 2013-08-29 on that basis. An auditor decoding the identifier should expect the UTC date to fall on the following day. Held privately by the studio: the 2008-2009 correspondence, receipts, and photographs. Selected private items can be promoted to public evidence as redaction and rights review are completed.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r8b4 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "The consignment engagement is corroborated by inbound 2008 correspondence from Sotheby's Photographs (confirming intake logistics and naming the department administrator) and by a shared Hana, HI mailing address linking the consignor to the Sun & Rain Works domain receipts. Contemporaneous conceptual intent is evidenced by art-referential documentation (an Andy Warhol volume juxtaposed with the photograph in images sent to Sotheby's). Each item is scoped to what it shows: these evidence identity, consignment, intent, and the concept's public continuity — not a witnessed live-creation event, and not precedence over any later artist or event.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r8b5 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Part of the documentation described here has since been dated and published as a record in its own right. The art-referential documentation photographs — including the frame composing the print with a volume of Warhol's philosophy — carry camera-written Exif placing them on 2008-08-08, and their close-up of the print's verso agrees in four particulars with the public Sotheby's catalogue entry for lot 16. That material is no longer only studio-reported: see the documentation-photograph evidence record.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r8b6 crm:P14_carried_out_by mca:sun-and-rain-works;
    crm:P4_has_time-span _:b0_r8b7;
    a crm:E65_Creation;
    rdfs:label "Compilation of the auction-engagement evidence record".
_:b0_r8b7 crm:P82a_begin_of_the_begin "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>;
    crm:P82b_end_of_the_end "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>;
    a crm:E52_Time-Span;
    rdfs:label "2026".
_:b0_r9b0 crm:P2_has_type <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    crm:P75i_is_possessed_by mca:sun-and-rain-works;
    a crm:E30_Right;
    rdfs:label "CC BY 4.0".
_:b0_r9b1 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Evidence archive: the WTFIA source folder for www.wtfisart.com (2008-2009)";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300404670;
    crm:P72_has_language aat:300388277;
    a crm:E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation.
_:b0_r9b2 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "record:evidence-wtfia-2009";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300312355;
    a crm:E42_Identifier.
_:b0_r9b3 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Evidence status: studio-held, with self-describing file metadata. The dates given here are drawn from filesystem modification times and from the OLE document-summary metadata embedded in the Word files. They are internally consistent across the ninety-seven files in the folder, but they are reported by the files themselves and are not independently notarized; they should be read as the archive's own account of its dates. The press sources excerpted in 'IsItArt.doc' are independently verifiable at their published URLs. No checksums, file hashes, or custody identifiers are published at this time. The same storage medium also holds an unrelated 2009 website project on renewable energy, 'Growing Aloha'; it is outside the boundary of this evidence archive.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r9b4 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Embedded document metadata, as recorded by the files themselves: 'IsItArt.doc' gives author Joseph M. Chirum, created 2009-01-22T03:03, last saved 2009-01-28T21:23, revision 21, total editing time 09:46, 14 pages, 4,049 words, 23,082 characters; its Title field carries the string 'August 13, 2007', which is a metadata field value and not, by itself, evidence of a 2007 document. 'Photographers.doc' gives author Joseph M. Chirum, created 2009-01-22T04:19, last saved 2009-01-26T04:15, revision 4, 1 page, 69 words. 'OldMasters.doc' gives created 2009-01-23T18:22, last saved 2009-01-26T20:50, revision 19, 8 pages, 1,263 words. 'Modern.doc' gives created 2009-01-27T13:15, last saved 2009-01-28T03:49, revision 10, and was produced with a different word processor from the other three. A second contributor is recorded in the metadata of all four documents: as the named author of both dealer-network directories, 'OldMasters.doc' and 'Modern.doc', and as the last editor of all four files. That person's name is withheld from this public record pending their consent, and is retained in the studio's private copy; the attribution of the two directories is theirs, not the studio principal's.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r9b5 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "The folder is named for the 'WTF is Art' concept and holds the material Sun & Rain Works assembled for www.wtfisart.com: the art-market press compilation, the photographer note, and the two dealer-network directories of galleries and their web addresses that were built as the site's link content. Its art-market compilation is the documented source context for the image study Art Market Reform, and the dealer directories are a documented instance of the project's stated interest in an archaeology of the art world. The folder holds no HTML: the built pages of www.wtfisart.com are not among these files, so the folder evidences what was made for the site, not what the site published or when it went live. The folder also contains an Ansel Adams reference image dated 2009-01-21 and a photographer reference note dated 2009-01-25; these show that Ansel Adams and photographic authorship were present in the same 2009 working set, and nothing further. The 2009 Sotheby's consignment is evidenced separately, in the auction-engagement evidence record. Each item here is scoped to what it shows.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
